        <briefdescription>
<para>Publish an id or a liveness word to lock-free readers. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Readers walk these two arrays without any lock, so a writer that assigns to them plainly races even while holding the write lock <ndash/> the lock excludes other writers, not readers. Release stores here pair with the acquire and relaxed loads on the read side. On x86-64 both are a plain MOV; the atomic_ref only constrains the compiler, not the hardware. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
